WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.050
Welcome to Part 1 of the implementation
series for provider notices.

2
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:09.112
One thing first: Provider Notices,
An Implementation Guide, is a draft.

3
00:00:09.112 --> 00:00:13.038
It's awaiting the owner's review, so
check it again after that review.

4
00:00:13.038 --> 00:00:15.425
The guide's premise fits in one line.

5
00:00:15.425 --> 00:00:18.829
Every provider tells you, in
writing and ahead of time,

6
00:00:18.829 --> 00:00:22.000
what it will change, retire
or patch in your tenant.

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.663
The gap is that nobody reads
it, owns it or closes it.

8
00:00:25.663 --> 00:00:28.451
The guide closes that gap in seven gates.

9
00:00:28.451 --> 00:00:33.374
Part 1 covers the orientation and
the four collection gates for Azure

10
00:00:33.374 --> 00:00:38.638
Service Health, Microsoft 365, Oracle
Cloud Infrastructure and AWS Health.

11
00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:41.924
Part 2 covers Google
Cloud, routing to owners,

12
00:00:41.924 --> 00:00:46.188
the digest and the evidence,
then the dangers and rollback.

13
00:00:46.188 --> 00:00:50.622
For each gate you'll see the steps, what
the kit really prints on its fixtures,

14
00:00:50.622 --> 00:00:54.413
the federal requirement, the
evidence and the government cloud.

15
00:00:54.413 --> 00:00:59.980
The kit's code is illustrative, tested
against fixtures, not against a live tenant.
